# VITE_API_URL is baked into the bundle at BUILD TIME and executed in the user's BROWSER.
# It must NOT be localhost — even if the backend runs on the same physical server, the
# browser resolves "localhost" against the visitor's own machine, not the server.
#
# Use a RELATIVE path so requests hit the same origin the app was served from (no CORS,
# no hardcoded scheme/host). It must NOT include "/api": endpoints already start with
# /api/v1 (see src/api/base.js and each module's BASE_PATH).
#   - app served at the domain ROOT (e.g. https://aulas.fis.unam.mx)              -> VITE_API_URL=
#   - app served under a SUBPATH (nginx maps /~aulas_icf/ -> front, /~aulas_icf/api -> Spring)
#     -> must be exactly that prefix (empty would hit /api/v1 OUTSIDE the proxy)  -> VITE_API_URL=/~aulas_icf
VITE_API_URL=/~aulas_icf